vice.","context":"Value-added services.5 Revenues from value-added services in the second quarter of 2026 were RMB369.0 million (US$54.4 million), compared with RMB491.2 million in the same period of 2025. The decrease was primarily due to a decrease in credit solutions revenues.","section":"","block":35,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-356976","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-19","reportDate":"2026-08-19","cik":"0001838413","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1838413/000119312526356976/d240729dex991.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4f86dcd909b3f8220fd8e01abf0b3b8ecd7120b8dbabab789bdcb05a393d50cb.bin","sha256":"4f86dcd909b3f8220fd8e01abf0b3b8ecd7120b8dbabab789bdcb05a393d50cb"}},{"id":"d0d05c53bdf368da43b56eed71559ebeb0e1ec78b5022553ea4152b1b984e10c","quote":"Sales and Marketing Expenses. Sales and marketing expenses in the second quarter of 2026 were RMB455.4 million (US$67.1 million), compared with RMB433.8 million in the same period of 2025. The increase was primarily due to additional investments in user ecosystem enhancement and user rights protection, partially offset by efficiency-focused spending on user acquisition.","context":"Cost of Revenues (including VAT net of government grants of RMB918.7 million and RMB602.2 million for the three months ended June 30, 2025 and 2026, respectively). Cost of revenues in the second quarter of 2026 was RMB925.9 million (US$136.5 million), compared with RMB1,238.4 million in the same period of 2025, primarily due to decreases in VAT, related tax surcharges and other tax costs, net of grants from government authorities. These tax-related costs net of government grants totaled RMB743.4 million, compared with RMB1,087.1 million in the same period of 2025, primarily due to a decrease in tax costs net of government grants related to the Company’s freight brokerage service.","section":"","block":36,"table":null,"attribution"